+	select FB_CFB_COPYAREA
+	select FB_CFB_IMAGEBLIT
+	select FB_IOMEM_FOPS
+	help
+	  Framebuffer support for the non-PnP Cirrus GD5440 behind the NEC
+	  PC-9821 Core-Graph bridge. The driver performs the PC-98-specific
+	  display routing and relocated-register initialization that the generic
+	  PCI cirrusfb driver cannot do.
+
+	  The driver provides 640x480 24-bpp, 800x600 16-bpp and 1024x768
+	  8-bpp modes with a 1 MiB linear /dev/fb device. It deliberately has no
+	  hardware module alias: build it as a module to keep the native PC-98
+	  GDC text console active during boot, then load pc98cirrusfb explicitly
+	  after confirming that the machine has the supported Core-Graph path.
+	  PCI GD75xx laptop LCD controllers are not supported.
+
+config FB_PC98_TRIDENT
+	tristate "NEC PC-9821 built-in Trident TGUI96xx framebuffer"
+	depends on FB && X86_PC9800 && PCI && HAS_IOPORT
+	depends on !FB_TRIDENT
+	select FB_SYSMEM_HELPERS_DEFERRED
+	help
+	  Framebuffer support for NEC Mate R systems with the on-board PCI
+	  Trident TGUI9660/9680/9682. The driver handles the PC-98-specific
+	  BAR1 register MMIO, CR21 linear aperture, mode initialization and
+	  display relay which the generic tridentfb driver does not support.
+
+	  This implementation provides 640x480 8-bpp through a shadow
+	  framebuffer. It paces and verifies writes to the linear aperture
+	  because Ra hardware can drop back-to-back CPU writes during scanout.
+
+	  Build it as a module to retain the GDC text console during boot. The
+	  module intentionally has no PCI hotplug alias; load pc98tridentfb
+	  explicitly when a framebuffer application or X server needs it.
 
 config FB_PM2
 	tristate "Permedia2 support"
